1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,981
Travel experts just named it the destination of the year for 2027.

2
00:00:05,251 --> 00:00:08,406
This is India, known as the Land of Spices.

3
00:00:08,676 --> 00:00:10,233
Its capital is New Delhi.

4
00:00:10,503 --> 00:00:17,275
About 1.47 billion people live here, on about 3,287,000 square kilometers.

5
00:00:17,545 --> 00:00:19,046
They speak Hindi and Bengali.

6
00:00:19,316 --> 00:00:20,967
Hello is namaste.

7
00:00:21,237 --> 00:00:23,108
Or, in Bengali, nomoshkar.

8
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:25,023
And they pay with the Indian rupee.

9
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:32,967
Some fun facts. And stay until the end, for a mystery nobody ever solved.

10
00:00:34,483 --> 00:00:40,085
Chess was born in India. Around the sixth century, a game called chaturanga spread from here across the world.

11
00:00:40,635 --> 00:00:49,775
Indian Railways carries about 23 million passengers every day. That is more than the whole population of the Netherlands.

12
00:00:50,325 --> 00:00:57,002
The Kumbh Mela is one of the largest peaceful gatherings on Earth, where millions of pilgrims come to bathe in sacred rivers.

13
00:00:57,967 --> 00:00:59,636
Some surprising places.

14
00:01:01,183 --> 00:01:09,093
Chand Baori, in Rajasthan, is a stepwell with 3,500 steps, going down 13 stories into the ground.

15
00:01:09,643 --> 00:01:16,876
In Meghalaya, people guide the roots of living fig trees across rivers, to grow bridges that last for centuries.

16
00:01:17,426 --> 00:01:24,459
The Kailasa temple at Ellora was carved from the top down, out of one single rock, in the eighth century.

17
00:01:25,009 --> 00:01:32,317
Jal Mahal, in Jaipur, is a palace in the middle of a lake. Only one floor shows. Four are underwater.

18
00:01:33,267 --> 00:01:35,979
So, what does ten dollars get you here?

19
00:01:37,450 --> 00:01:39,440
A cup of masala chai costs about 16 cents.

20
00:01:39,990 --> 00:01:45,132
A vada pav, the street burger of Mumbai, is about 21 cents.

21
00:01:45,682 --> 00:01:48,218
A local thali meal is about $1.60.

22
00:01:48,768 --> 00:01:52,351
A sleeper train ticket from Delhi to Varanasi is about $5.

23
00:01:52,901 --> 00:01:55,577
And an auto rickshaw ride across town is about $2.

24
00:01:56,127 --> 00:02:06,764
But some things cost more than at home. A new iPhone 18 Pro is about $1,700 in India, compared to about $1,200 in the United States.

25
00:02:07,314 --> 00:02:17,868
So with $10, you get chai, a vada pav, a thali, a train ticket, and a rickshaw ride, and you still have about a dollar left.

26
00:02:18,833 --> 00:02:20,045
Now, the don’t list.

27
00:02:21,583 --> 00:02:27,059
Don’t bring a vape. E cigarettes are banned in India, and you can face up to one year in prison.

28
00:02:27,609 --> 00:02:34,162
Don’t take photos near military sites, airports, or railway stations without care. Officials warn that it can cause trouble.

29
00:02:34,712 --> 00:02:38,388
Don’t wear your shoes inside a temple or someone's home. Take them off at the door.

30
00:02:38,938 --> 00:02:47,922
Don’t order beef in most of the north, because killing cows is banned in most states. And some states, like Gujarat and Bihar, ban alcohol.

31
00:02:48,472 --> 00:02:55,884
And don’t ever go near North Sentinel Island. It is illegal to come within five nautical miles, to protect the people who live there.

32
00:02:56,833 --> 00:02:58,147
Let's talk about culture.

33
00:02:59,683 --> 00:03:05,617
Hyderabadi biryani layers rice and spiced meat, then seals them in one pot to cook slowly.

34
00:03:06,167 --> 00:03:12,270
The sari is a single long piece of cloth, draped around the body, and worn for many centuries.

35
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:18,208
The sitar is a long necked string instrument, famous around the world for its shimmering sound.

36
00:03:19,167 --> 00:03:20,161
Time for a little history.

37
00:03:21,683 --> 00:03:30,383
In 1947, India became independent from Britain. But the country was split in two, and the Partition forced millions of people to flee their homes.

38
00:03:30,933 --> 00:03:36,901
In 1991, India opened its economy to the world, and the country began to change fast.

39
00:03:37,451 --> 00:03:44,178
And in 2023, its Chandrayaan-3 probe landed near the Moon’s south pole, a first for any country.

40
00:03:45,133 --> 00:03:49,797
And now, the chapter you were all waiting for: legends and mysteries.

41
00:03:51,316 --> 00:03:57,436
Kuldhara, near Jaisalmer, was a prosperous village founded around the 13th century.

42
00:03:57,986 --> 00:04:01,959
Then, one night in the early 1800s, every family left.

43
00:04:02,508 --> 00:04:08,713
Legend says a corrupt minister wanted the chief's daughter, so the villagers fled and cursed the place.

44
00:04:09,262 --> 00:04:13,352
Others blame an earthquake, or a lack of water. Nobody knows for sure.

45
00:04:13,901 --> 00:04:20,865
Bhangarh Fort, in Rajasthan, is said to be one of the most haunted places in India.

46
00:04:21,414 --> 00:04:25,240
One legend says an ascetic cursed the town. Another tells of a princess and a magician.

47
00:04:25,789 --> 00:04:31,154
Today, a government sign forbids anyone from entering between sunset and sunrise.

48
00:04:31,704 --> 00:04:34,286
Why the town was abandoned is still debated.

49
00:04:34,836 --> 00:04:40,896
High in the Himalayas, at about 5,000 meters, lies Roopkund, the Skeleton Lake.

50
00:04:41,445 --> 00:04:44,828
Hundreds of human skeletons lie around its shore.

51
00:04:45,377 --> 00:04:52,771
DNA tests showed they were not one group. Some came from the eastern Mediterranean, and died around the 19th century.

52
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:57,842
Why they were there, on a remote mountain pass, remains a mystery.

53
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,069
That was India.

54
00:05:02,339 --> 00:05:05,172
Which country should we visit next? Tell me in the comments.
